          "title": "NJ Anti-Eviction Act: good cause required to evict",
          "requirement": "A landlord must have good cause to evict a residential tenant, and may not evict or fail to renew a written or oral lease without good cause. The landlord must prove the grounds in court. Possession may be recovered only by tenant consent or through the legal eviction process.",
          "citation": "N.J.S.A. 2A:18-53",
          "source_url": "https://www.nj.gov/dca/codes/publications/pdf_lti/t_i_r.pdf",
          "quoted_span": "good cause to evict a tenant (N.J.S.A. 2A:18-53).",
