          "title": "NJ Anti-Eviction Act: Notice to Quit required for good cause evictions",
          "requirement": "A Notice to Quit is required for all good cause evictions except eviction for nonpayment of rent. Each cause other than nonpayment must be described in detail in a written notice to the tenant. A Judgment for Possession must still be entered by the court before the tenant must move.",
